From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 23:29:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2477/3799] soh: rename func_80A03AB0 -> EnElf_RunMotion

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence HIGH) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: runs the current motion function, first updating the targeting colour when that flag is set
Defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Elf/z_en_elf.c.

Tagged [LLM:HIGH] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Elf/z_en_elf.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Elf/z_en_elf.c b/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Elf/z_en_elf.c
index 15f830ef8..26a5fdae6 100644
--- a/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Elf/z_en_elf.c
+++ b/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Elf/z_en_elf.c
@@ -820,7 +820,8 @@ void EnElf_HealPopOut(EnElf* this, PlayState* play) {
     Audio_PlayActorSound2(&this->actor, NA_SE_EV_FIATY_HEAL - SFX_FLAG);
 }
 
-void func_80A03AB0(EnElf* this, PlayState* play) {
+// LLM generated name (HIGH), was func_80A03AB0: runs the current motion function, first updating the targeting colour when that flag is set
+void EnElf_RunMotion(EnElf* this, PlayState* play) {
     if (this->fairyFlags & 4) {
         func_80A04414(this, play);
     }
@@ -871,7 +872,7 @@ void func_80A03CF8(EnElf* this, PlayState* play) {
     f32 distFromLinksHead;
 
     func_80A0461C(this, play);
-    func_80A03AB0(this, play);
+    EnElf_RunMotion(this, play);  // was func_80A03AB0 [LLM:HIGH]
 
     xScale = 0.0f;
 
@@ -1256,7 +1257,7 @@ void func_80A04DE4(EnElf* this, PlayState* play) {
         this->fairyFlags &= ~0x10;
     }
 
-    func_80A03AB0(this, play);
+    EnElf_RunMotion(this, play);  // was func_80A03AB0 [LLM:HIGH]
     headCopy = this->actor.focus.pos;
 
     EnElf_FlyToTargetClamped(this, &headCopy, 0, 20.0f, 0.2f);  // was func_80A03148 [LLM:HIGH]
